(1) DO COMPARABLE FAMILIES BLOCK ALL SEVEN MODULI?
    4000 random comparable 13-families: block all seven in 433 (10.8%)
    => the sieve already kills ~89% of comparable families outright.

(2) DO ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS BLOCK ALL SEVEN?  (small doubling ~2)
    2000 random APs: block all seven in 611 (30.6%)
    an AP has doubling 1.92 (minimal)

(3) THE DECISIVE TEST: among families that BLOCK all seven, is the
    doubling forced UP?  (tension would mean blockers cannot be additively structured)
    blockers    : n=732, median doubling 6.92
    non-blockers: n=5268, median doubling 6.92

(4) CAN A FAMILY HAVE BOTH minimal doubling AND block all seven?
    YES -- explicit APs (doubling 2.00, the additive minimum) blocking all seven:
      a=665, d=53: [665, 718, 771, 824]...  doubling 1.92
      a=1927, d=137: [1927, 2064, 2201, 2338]...  doubling 1.92
      a=259, d=49: [259, 308, 357, 406]...  doubling 1.92

    => NO TENSION.  The multiplicative sieve constraint and minimal
       additive doubling are SIMULTANEOUSLY satisfiable, by explicit
       arithmetic progressions.  The over-determination hope FAILS.
